TEAM-4251 acceptance item 15 / part A — Playwright smoke at repo HEAD 5fa3728
branch feature/TEAM-4251-qa-verifier

RUN CONDITIONS (both matter, and neither is documented in the repo):
  1. playwright.config.ts has NO `webServer` block, so `npm test` requires a Next
     server to already be listening. With nothing running, all 38 tests fail in
     ~5ms each with "connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3000" — an empty-looking
     38/38 failure that has nothing to do with the app.
  2. The chromium browser binary is not pre-installed in this sandbox; without
     `npx playwright install chromium`, 32 of the 38 fail with
     "browserType.launch: Executable doesn't exist".
  So: server on :3111 (`npx next dev -p 3111`, PLAYWRIGHT_BASE_URL set),
  chromium installed, .env.local copied from .env.example.

RESULT:  23 passed  ·  8 skipped  ·  7 failed  ·  EXIT=1   (2.6m, 1 worker)
  Reproduced identically twice (once on :3000, once on :3111) and matches the
  count the TEAM-4249 frontend dev reported.

=====================================================================
CLASSIFICATION OF EACH FAILURE
The dev's claim under review: "7 failures, all AWS AccessDenied from the sandbox
IAM role in untouched src/app/api/** handlers."
VERDICT: 6 of 7 confirmed. #7 is NOT an IAM denial — it is a missing-env 500.
=====================================================================

The sandbox principal for every denial below:
  arn:aws:sts::838829463875:assumed-role/agentcore-hub-coding-runtime-role/
  BedrockAgentCore-96193f1a-737e-4f77-9c9d-10eb60c51b33

Denials counted in the dev-server log for this run:
    163  AccessDeniedException
     45  AccessDenied
     33  not authorized to perform: logs:DescribeLogGroups
     30  not authorized to perform: cloudwatch:ListMetrics
      7  not authorized to perform: bedrock-agentcore:ListHarnesses
      7  not authorized to perform: bedrock-agentcore:ListAgentRuntimes
      1  not authorized to perform: dynamodb:Scan

1) e2e-api-routes.spec.ts:14  "Agents API returns discovered agents"
   Assertion: expect(agents.length).toBeGreaterThan(0)  ->  Received: 0
   CONFIRMED AccessDenied. /api/agentcore/agents returns HTTP 200 with `[]`
   (it swallows the error), and the denial behind the empty array is:
     "...is not authorized to perform: bedrock-agentcore:ListAgentRuntimes on
      resource: arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-east-1:838829463875:runtime/*
      because no identity-based policy allows the
      bedrock-agentcore:ListAgentRuntimes action"
   Untouched by TEAM-4246/47/48/49.

2) e2e-api-routes.spec.ts:28  "Agents API includes harness agents"
   Assertion: expect(harness).toBeTruthy()  ->  Received: undefined
   CONFIRMED AccessDenied, sibling of #1:
     "...is not authorized to perform: bedrock-agentcore:ListHarnesses on
      resource: arn:aws:bedrock-agentcore:us-east-1:838829463875:harness/*
      because no identity-based policy allows the
      bedrock-agentcore:ListHarnesses action"
   Untouched.

3) e2e-api-routes.spec.ts:66  "Metrics API returns usage data"
   Assertion: expect(res.status()).toBe(200)  ->  Received: 500
   CONFIRMED AccessDenied. /api/agentcore/metrics fans out to CloudWatch:
     "...is not authorized to perform: cloudwatch:ListMetrics because no
      identity-based policy allows the cloudwatch:ListMetrics action"
     "...is not authorized to perform: logs:DescribeLogGroups on resource:
      arn:aws:logs:us-east-1:838829463875:log-group::log-stream: because no
      identity-based policy allows the logs:DescribeLogGroups action"
   Untouched.

4) tab-agents.spec.ts:15  "shows agent cards when discovery completes"
   Assertion: getByText('Discovering agents...') expected visible, not found (5s)
   CONFIRMED AccessDenied, downstream of #1/#2 — the page finished discovery
   with zero agents, so neither the cards nor the loading text is on screen.
   This is the spec's own fallback branch, not an app error. Untouched.

5) tab-dashboard.spec.ts:33  "shows agent performance table with live data"
   Assertion: locator('table') expected visible, element(s) not found
   CONFIRMED AccessDenied, downstream of #1/#2/#3 — no agents and no metrics
   means no performance table is rendered. Untouched.

6) tab-workflow.spec.ts:45  "workflow list loads from API"
   Assertion: expect(listRes.ok()).toBeTruthy()  ->  Received: false
   CONFIRMED AccessDenied. GET /api/workflow/list returns HTTP 500 with:
     {"error":"Failed to list workflows: User: ...assumed-role/
      agentcore-hub-coding-runtime-role/... is not authorized to perform:
      dynamodb:Scan on resource: arn:aws:dynamodb:us-east-1:838829463875:table/
      agentcore-hub-workflows because no identity-based policy allows the
      dynamodb:Scan action","workflows":[]}
   src/app/api/workflow/list/route.ts is untouched by the epic.

7) tab-workflow.spec.ts:220  "cancel button + modal flow on a fresh workflow"
   Assertion: expect(startRes.ok()).toBeTruthy()  ->  Received: false
   *** REFUTES the dev's blanket classification. *** Not an IAM denial at all —
   POST /api/workflow/start returns 500 with a CONFIG validation message:
     workflow/start failed: 500 {"error":"Jira Cloud provider requires
     JIRA_SITE_URL, JIRA_EMAIL, JIRA_API_TOKEN, and JIRA_PROJECT_KEY
     environment variables."}
   Cause: .env.example ships TICKET_PROVIDER=jira (line 76) with no JIRA_*
   credentials, and this workspace's .env.local is a copy of it. The request
   never reaches AWS — it is rejected by the ticket-provider guard.
   Caveat, stated plainly: this failure is a property of MY .env.local, so the
   dev may legitimately have seen a different 7th failure if their .env.local
   set TICKET_PROVIDER=dynamodb. Either way the classification "all 7 are AWS
   AccessDenied" is not accurate for this configuration, and the run is not
   evidence about the epic's code either way.

